    "related_formalizations": [
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/plby/Erdos90",
        "note": "Boris Alexeev's Lean formalization of OpenAI's 2026 counterexample, announced on the Lean Zulip and verified on lean-eval on 2026-06-26. He reports that Codex produced it over about a month with himself as the one person in the loop.\nIt proves the fixed-power statement, and proves it outright: the class field theory is formalized rather than assumed, the proof path carries no sorries, and the repository's three axiom declarations, which state Remark II.3.12 of Milne's \"Class Field Theory\", are in a module the proof does not import.\nHe reports 1.2 million lines in the formalization, of which roughly 800,000 are imported by the final result and 10,000 to 40,000 are the novel part of the argument.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      },
      {
        "identifier": "https://github.com/logical-intelligence/erdos-unit-distance",
        "note": "Logical Intelligence's Lean 4 formalization of the same result, produced with Aleph Prover, announced on 2026-05-28 at roughly 33,000 lines. It also reaches the fixed-power statement, that {n : 0 < n and nu(n) >= n^(1+delta)} is infinite for some delta > 0, by way of class field towers.\nIt is conditional, deliberately and visibly: `main_theorem` takes the Golod-Shafarevich inequality and Shafarevich's relation-rank bound as hypotheses in its signature rather than formalizing them. Neither work uses the other.",
        "relationship": "independent"
      }
    ],
